Subject: [PATCH] SableOS: Step n of N on every owner setup step
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Setup design (sable-setup-wizard-titan2): "First boot · step 3 of 8"
on each screen.

sable/SableSteps (pure) numbers the owner flow in eight steps:
Welcome, Language, Wi-Fi, Privacy, Theme, Date and location, Screen
lock, Ready. Screens that only appear on some phones or in some states
(keyboard help, SIM missing, recovery update, navigation, restore once
validated) carry the number of the step they belong to, so the count
never changes during setup. Without a Wi-Fi step (no Wi-Fi and no
telephony, or online through Ethernet) the flow has seven steps and the
later numbers move up. Bluetooth and device extras have no number.

BaseSetupWizardActivity shows "Step n of N" in the layout's sable_step
line, else in a line it adds above the Glif header title. Only the
owner flow is numbered; secondary-user and work-profile flows show no
line. Any failure leaves the step as it was.

Wi-Fi and screen lock are Settings screens the wizard opens, and they
cannot show the line, so SubBaseActivity says it in a toast as they
open. For Wi-Fi the toast adds the password hint "Alt/Sym for symbols ·
software keyboard fallback" (the Q25 has no Fn key). Welcome's
Accessibility and Emergency screens are not steps and show no toast.

